From fa5118b1b048337bab13f3dfe2e35fc749368688 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sasha Levin <sashal@kernel.org>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 14:01:32 -0700
Subject: x86/cpuid: Mark CPUID function 0x23 as being indexed

From: Sean Christopherson <seanjc@google.com>

[ Upstream commit 108775fa28fe04a16f19a828a779689f3d0ea9f0 ]

Add function 0x23 to the set of CPUID functions that are indexed, as per
the SDM and the many sub-leafs defined in leaf_types.h.

Closes: https://lore.kernel.org/all/213d614fe73e183a230c8f4e0c8fa1cc3d45df39.camel@intel.com
Reported-by: Rick Edgecombe <rick.p.edgecombe@intel.com>
Signed-off-by: Sean Christopherson <seanjc@google.com>
Signed-off-by: Borislav Petkov (AMD) <bp@alien8.de>
Tested-by: Rick Edgecombe <rick.p.edgecombe@intel.com>
Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20261022210134.612848-2-seanjc@google.com
[ sashal: Added case 0x23: to the older cpuid.h header, since the cpuid/api.h file doesn't exist here, and the trailing context differs because case 0x24: is absent. ]
Signed-off-by: Sasha Levin <sashal@kernel.org>
---
 arch/x86/include/asm/cpuid.h | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/x86/include/asm/cpuid.h b/arch/x86/include/asm/cpuid.h
index 9bee3e7bf9736..148dd9645abea 100644
--- a/arch/x86/include/asm/cpuid.h
+++ b/arch/x86/include/asm/cpuid.h
@@ -143,6 +143,7 @@ static __always_inline bool cpuid_function_is_indexed(u32 function)
 	case 0x1d:
 	case 0x1e:
 	case 0x1f:
+	case 0x23:
 	case 0x8000001d:
 		return true;
 	}
-- 
